Generate src/checked.rs: additive reusable checked mathematical capabilities.
Preserve all legacy modules and types. Depend only on existing Coefficient,
Polynomial, computation Budget/Error, scalar and tensor contracts; no providers.
All arithmetic must use checked coefficient/polynomial calls with shared Budget.
Expose generic const-size matrix identity/add/sub/mul/scale/trace/transpose.
Preflight matrix dimensions/work and coefficient bits before cloning output.
Fallible sigma/barsigma/gamma validate indices before constructing constant
entries; build constants directly and negate through checked coefficient calls.
Generic RationalFunction<A> has private numerator and nonzero denominator;
construction validates via existing polynomial engine. Add/sub/mul/div/neg,
residual and evaluation retain original domains without cancelling factors.
Division must retain the divisor denominator restriction by multiplying both
result numerator and denominator by that denominator. Reject zero divisors.
Residual zero is equality only on the common domain, never domain equality.
Generic commuting polynomial spinor determinant bracket and Schouten; checked
coefficient BCFW shift validates leg indices and stages updates atomically.
Selected typed tensor wrapper: budgeted metric compatibility and declaration,
delegating Context validation. Do not wrap tensor expression arithmetic, whose
legacy coefficients still use panicking operators. No catch_unwind.
Independent tests cover large BigC, explicit independent gamma matrices,
Schouten component identities, poles including quotient domain preservation,
invalid indices/zero divisors and resource failures. No chapter dispatch.
Document limits: deterministic budgets not OOM/time limits, trusted Coefficient
implementations must obey their trait contract; no full tensor migration/CAS.

Tensor declaration MUST preflight conservative closure work and storage against
shared Budget before Context::declare: rank<=8; None group bound=1, built-in
symmetric/antisymmetric bound=n!, arbitrary signed generators bound=2*n!
(identity with negative sign is legal). Charge closure comparison/permutation
work and transient storage conservatively before allocation. Track aggregate
successful declaration count, conservative group-entry count and retained
name/slot/group storage bytes privately across calls, even with renewed budgets.
Check combined declaration+group Terms and storage InputBytes before mutation.
Only commit counters after successful underlying declaration. Failed preflight
or Context validation/orbit exhaustion leaves registry and counters unchanged;
Budget work already spent need not roll back. Existing orbit_steps is an
additional per-declaration cap. No OS-allocation/time guarantee.
